    description: "**Found by the independent I/O allowlist gate (WI-vumum, `scripts/check-io-allowlist`).** For human decision — touches governance (ALLOWED_WEBSITES.md), so no implementation without approval.\n\n`hypergumbo_tracker.stop_hook._call_openrouter` POSTs to OpenRouter (constant https URL) with `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` when that variable is set, sending the text of unread human tracker messages that start with `[[preface]]` (WI-mofaz precedence gate). It runs from the stop hook (`tracker guidance`), i.e. inside agent sessions.\n\n`openrouter.ai` does not appear in ALLOWED_WEBSITES.md (case-insensitive grep, 2026-10-10). AGENTS.md: \"Any network access must be limited to the allowlisted domains in ALLOWED_WEBSITES.md.\" The code path is dormant without the key, so this is a policy disagreement, not an observed violation.\n\nOptions: (a) add openrouter.ai to ALLOWED_WEBSITES.md with the use-case (governance edit, human approval); (b) remove/disable the outbound call; (c) document that the key must not be set in agent sessions."  # 1d14
